    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, when you say \"the consensus has shifted\" it sounds like you're saying the inequality part is the most important thing to focus on now. but if the primary goal of those policies was to fix the macro economy and stop inflation, doesn't that make them a success by definition? isn't it kind of unfair to judge them based on social factors they weren't necessarily designed to address?",
