      "content": "You make a valid point. The primary policy goal of deregulation was to address macroeconomic issues like inflation, which was a major concern at the time. In this context, the success of these policies can be measured by their ability to bring down inflation and stimulate economic growth, which they did. Judging these policies solely on their social outcomes, like increased income inequality, may not be entirely fair or accurate. Long-term, evidence-based assessments may need to take into account both macroeconomic and social outcomes.",
